    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThe entire site is available for sale. Please ignore the temporary fence in the photos and video.\n\nFeaturing magnificent sea views over Dublin Bay towards Howth and Dalkey Hill, Gort Na Mona boasts tremendous charm and character. Built in 1903 the house benefits from a unique elevated site of approximately 0.41 acres of prime land. Home to the same family since the 1980's, the residence currently comprises 3 reception rooms, 6 bedrooms & 4 bathrooms. In addition, there is a basement room which would make an ideal home office and is currently used for storage. There is an attractive front garden boasting a myriad of attractive plants, bushes and mature trees. Planning permission was granted in December 2024 to open up a driveway to the front - Reference D24A/0728.\n\nThe forecourt provides ample parking for 6 cars. A side gate leads to the magnificent rear garden, showing the rooftops of Silchester Park and impressive views of the sea. Although in need up updating throughout, the property offers tremendous potential to be transformed into a beautiful modern family home in this established neighbourhood within easy reach of all the amenities of Glasthule, Sandycove and Dalkey villages. Alternatively, the magnificent house & gardens offer tremendous scope for a Developer to construct a small scheme subject to obtaining the necessary planning permission. The location of this home makes it the perfect place for those looking to establish themselves on one of Dublin's most desirable and sought-after addresses.\n\nIt offers easy access to DART and bus services. This well established area boasts a wealth of amenities including top class restaurants, bistros, pubs, shops and boutiques. Also within walking distance are the famous Forty Foot bathing areas at Sandycove, Dalkey/Killiney Hill, tennis, golf, football and GAA clubs. Some of Dublin's most renowned primary and secondary schools are all within easy reach. Dun Laoghaire is nearby with its ever walkable piers, the People's Park (which hosts a farmer's market every Sunday) and numerous shops and restaurants in the town.\n\nThe recently constructed cycle track connects Sandycove with Blackrock. The four yacht clubs and extensive marina at Dun Laoghaire Harbour will be of major interest to the marine and sailing enthusiasts. The convenience and desirability of this house and its location cannot be overstated. It must be viewed to really appreciate its quality, elevation and wonderful position."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorched Entrance - \nwith door to the\n\nReception Hall - 4.1m x 2.1m\nwith solid timber floor, understairs telephone alcove, ceiling coving and door to\n\nBoot Room - 2.7m x 2.2m\nwith herringbone solid stained pine floor and fitted shelving\n\nBreakfast Room - 3.05m x 4m\nwith picture rail, alcove for a Range, opening through to the kitchen and door to\n\nInner Lobby - 1.2m x 2.7m\nwith door out to an enclosed utility and sliding door opens to\n\nGuest W.C. - \nwith wash hand basin and picture rail\n\nBoiler House/Hot Press - 2.1m x 2.7m\nwith industrial oil fired central heating boiler, large sink unit with drainer to the side, shelving under, tall water cylinder, immersion, heating controls & timer\n\nUtility/Sunroom - 4.3m x 5.5m\nwith glazed door opening in and shower room, tiled floor, storage heater, pedestrian side door leading out to the front and aluminium clad double glazed door opening out to the rear garden\n\nShower Room - \nwith step in tiled Triton shower, w.c., pedestal wash hand basin, tiled floor, part tiled walls and recessed lighting\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.4m x 3.5m\nwith solid timber floor, Dimplex storage heater, dual aspect windows looking over the front garden and skylight\n\nKitchen - 3.4m x 2.25m\nwith a range of fitted painted press units, one and a half bowl single drainer stainless steel sink unit, drawers, worktops, space for stand alone cooker, tiled splashback, window overlooking the rear, and opening through to the\n\nDining/Family Room - 6.15m x 6.6m\nopen plan with solid timber floor, tri-aspect windows looking front, side and over the rear, coving, fireplace with brick surround, open fire, raised slate hearth and door opening into the\n\nHome Office - 4.6m x 4m\nwith solid timber herringbone floor, ceiling coving, window looking side with coloured stained glass over, and very attractive period fireplace with timber surround, tiled inset and hearth\n\nReception Room - 4.6m x 4.8m\nwith bay window overlooking front, ceiling coving, solid timber herringbone floor, exceptionally attractive marble fireplace with marble inset and hearth and wall sconces either side of the room\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - \n\n\nBathroom - \nwith corner bath, pedestal wash hand basin, bidet, tiled floor, part tiled walls, step in tiled Mira shower and pine timber panelled ceiling with recessed lighting\n\nSeparate Guest W.C. - \nwith shelving\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.15m x 2.8m\npicture window overlooking the stunning view over the rooftops across Dublin Bay to Howth\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.2m x 3.3m\nwith picture rail and views across Dublin Bay to Howth\n\nInner Lobby - \nwith opening through to\n\nDressing Area - 2m x 2.3m\n\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.85m x 6.6m\nwith dormer window looking out at the stunning view, window looking front and door to\n\nEn Suite Bathroom - \nwith bath, w.c., pedestal wash hand basin, fully tiled walls and floor, fitted mirror, recessed lighting, shaving socket and light\n\nBedroom 5 - 3.5m x 2.3m\nwith tongue & groove solid timber floor and louvered door wardrobes for storage\n\nShower Room - \nwith shower with oversized tray, tiled floor and tiled walls\n\nBedroom 6 - 4.7m x 5m\nwith bay window looking front with picture rail and blocked up fireplace\n\nBasement Landing - \nwith door from kitchen and stairs down to the\n\nBasement - 4.2m x 6.6m\noverlooks the rear with pedestrian door that opens out to the rear garden\n\n"
